gned for ages {age}. With {dots} dots, it suits children who can confidently count to {dots}; younger children can complete it with a little help.","faqQ2":"How do I print the {name} worksheet?","faqA2":"Click the download button to get the free PDF, then print it on regular paper (A4 or US Letter) from any browser or PDF reader. No special software is needed.","faqQ3":"Is the {name} printable really free?","faqA3":"Yes — it is 100% free, with no sign-up, account, or payment required. You may print it for home or classroom use."},"blogPage":{"eyebrow":"Learning resources","h1":"Dot to Dot Ideas for Parents and Teachers","description":"Practical guides for choosing activities, building early learning skills, and using printable worksheets at home or in the classroom.","breadcrumb":"Blog","latestEyebrow":"Latest articles","latestH2":"Helpful ideas you can use today","readArticle":"Read article","by":"By","backToAll":"← Back to all articles","savePinterest":"Save to Pinterest","relatedEyebrow":"Free printables","relatedHeading":"Try these dot to dot collections next"},"downloadButton":{"label":"Download Free Printable PDF","usage":"Free for home and classroom use.","paperNote":"Sized for {size} paper.","paperLetter":"US Letter","paperA4":"A4","alternateLink":"Prefer {size}? Download that version","downloadSize":"Download (Print Size: {size})"},"downloadBadge":{"downloaded":"Downloaded","times":"times","greatChoice":"You’ve made a great choice!"},"bookmarkButton":{"regionLabel":"Bookmark this page","shortcut":"Press <shortcut></shortcut> to bookmark!","dismiss":"Dismiss","shared":"Shared!","buttonAria":"Save or share this puzzle page","buttonTitle":"Save this puzzle","saved":"Saved!","save":"Save"},"languageSwitcher":{"label":"Language","selectLabel":"Select language"},"shareButtons":{"label":"Share","copyLink":"Copy link","copied":"Link copied!","shareMe":"Share me"},"bookmark":{"save":"Bookmark this page","saved":"Saved to bookmarks","labelText":"Bookmark this","hint"